{"name":"Jodhpurs","hex":"#ebdcb6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jodhpurs","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Flared riding trousers of heavy cloth, fitting tightly from knee to ankle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jodhpurs"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jodhpurs","blocks":[{"text":"Jodhpurs, in their modern form, are tight-fitting trousers to the ankle, where they end in a snug cuff, and are worn primarily for horse riding. The term is also used as slang for a type of short riding boot, also called a paddock boot or a jodhpur boot, because they are worn with jodhpurs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Horse_riding_in_coca_cola_arena_-_melbourne_show_2005.jpg/330px-Horse_riding_in_coca_cola_arena_-_melbourne_show_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jodhpurs","wikidata":"Q770562"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/MarwariHorseRajasthan.jpg/250px-MarwariHorseRajasthan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f4/MarwariHorseRajasthan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/MarwariHorseRajasthan.jpg/250px-MarwariHorseRajasthan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marwari horse in Rajasthan. Note the traditional long riding trousers, tight around the calf, reaching to Mojari slippers.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarwariHorseRajasthan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Jodhpurs_%28PSF%29.png/500px-Jodhpurs_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Jodhpurs_%28PSF%29.png/1280px-Jodhpurs_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Jodhpurs_%28PSF%29.png/500px-Jodhpurs_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Classic riding jodhpurs, showing the extra width in the thigh area, which allows for lateral leg movement when in the saddle.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJodhpurs_(PSF).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/HalfChaps1.jpg/500px-HalfChaps1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/HalfChaps1.jpg/500px-HalfChaps1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jodhpur boots, also called paddock boots, are worn with jodhpurs, but also may be worn with breeches if half-chaps are added which provide the functionality and look of a tall riding boot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalfChaps1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Cecil_B_DeMille_1937.JPG/500px-Cecil_B_DeMille_1937.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Cecil_B_DeMille_1937.JPG/500px-Cecil_B_DeMille_1937.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cecil B. DeMille, 1937, wearing the flared-hip riding breeches that are often termed jodhpurs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACecil_B_DeMille_1937.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Lindsey_on_horse.jpg/500px-Lindsey_on_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Lindsey_on_horse.jpg/1280px-Lindsey_on_horse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa